# Never commit credentials or run artifacts — this repo may be public.
# Match EVERY config variant, not just config.json: keeping one file per
# environment (config.sandbox.json / config.prod.json) is what stops a switch
# between tenants from overwriting the other environment's credentials, and
# those extra files must be ignored too or the fix becomes a leak.
config.json
config.*.json
!config.example.json
logs/
stats/
cache/

# Read-only preflight output — contains sampled CUSTOMER data (Zephyr/Jira responses).
preflight_shapes.json

# Write-ahead spool: fetched CUSTOMER results held on disk only until Qase
# confirms the write, then deleted. Must never be committed — it is raw customer
# execution data (statuses, comments, attachment hashes).
spool/
.spool/
*.spool.jsonl

# Captured browser session for attachment downloads — a full session credential.
zephyr_session.json
*_session.json
playwright_*_session.json

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Internal QA seeders — never ship in the public repo (they write junk data into a Zephyr tenant)
setup_test_data*.py

# Internal strategy/research notes — kept local (candid framing + third-party
# internal endpoints; not needed to run the script)
ATTACHMENTS-AUTOMATION.md
BACKLOG.md
